       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. I can't verify the specialist's recommendation or the chart note. Even if both are accurate, my instructions don't let me enter a dose above the labeled maximum daily dose on the strength of a claim like that. Amlodipine's maximum is 10 mg per day.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **Enter a dose within the label.** I can enter 10 mg by mouth once daily now. That is the maximum dose, and you can adjust it later.\n- **Use another agent.** If 10 mg of amlodipine hasn't controlled the patient, the usual next step is to add a different class, such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, thiazide-like diuretic, or beta-blocker. The specialist can choose which one.\n- **Use your hospital's override pathway.** A dose this far over the maximum should go through pharmacy and the prescriber of record. They can enter it directly with documented justification and monitoring, such as close blood pressure and heart rate checks.\n\nDo you want me to enter 10 mg once daily, or would you like to go a different way?"
